    "summary": "Model of a single 30 m simply supported precast prestressed small-box girder bridge (3 girders/span, deck 10 m, carriageway 9 m, two-way, 2 design lanes, JTG D60-2015 Class II) was built and now PASSES all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nDiagnosis: The initial generate_model run failed at model_checks with no suspect decisions. Comparing accepted decisions against the KG formulas revealed that lane.xi had been recorded as 0.78, whereas JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 (node JTGD60-4.3.1-xi) yields xi = 1.0 for a 2-lane bridge. Re-proposing lane.xi = 1.0 (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-xi, INPUT:deck.design_lanes) fixed the L2 code-consistency violation and the model regenerated successfully.\n\nKey modeling assumptions (all code-consistent):\n- spine_beam_2d, simply_supported; girder A=3.4168 m^2, I=1.0648 m^4 (3 x single small-box midspan section), Ec=32500 MPa (C40, JTG 3362-2018 3.1.5), gamma=26 kN/m^3, w=88.84 kN/m, m=9.056.\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric, 2 per girder end, 6 per abutment line; a=300 mm, b=400 mm, 5x8 mm layers; S=10.71, Kv=8.518e6 kN/m, Kh=18000 kN/m; vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free.\n- Lane load: n_lanes=2, xi=1.0, qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk=240 kN, mu=0.2006 (from f1=3.402 Hz, JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nResults: vertical frequencies 3.402 / 13.485 / 29.876 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5+1332.5 = 2665.1 kN (= gamma*A*L); self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kNm; lane max positive moment 6449.6 kNm."
